### 4. Native Binary Dependency `better-sqlite3` in `package.json` (HIGH)

#### Problem
In [`server/package.json:21`](file:///c:/Users/Ashwin/Desktop/LMS/server/package.json#L21), `"better-sqlite3": "^13.0.3"` and `"@prisma/adapter-better-sqlite3": "^7.10.0"` are listed as dependencies.
`better-sqlite3` is a compiled C++ binary module requiring `node-gyp`, Python, and make tools. It is not imported or used anywhere in the active codebase (Qualiva runs on PostgreSQL, MongoDB Atlas, and Prisma). If Render's Linux build container encounters a node-gyp or compiler mismatch, `npm install` will fail and abort the build.

#### Solution
Safely remove `"better-sqlite3"` and `"@prisma/adapter-better-sqlite3"` from [`server/package.json`](file:///c:/Users/Ashwin/Desktop/LMS/server/package.json) and synchronize `package-lock.json`.

---

### 5. Render Blueprint Configuration (`render.yaml`) (ENHANCEMENT)

#### Problem
Manually creating and configuring two separate services (Static Site for `client` and Web Service for `server`) in the Render web dashboard is error-prone. One wrong path or missing rewrite rule causes 404s.

#### Solution
Create a clean, standardized [`render.yaml`](file:///c:/Users/Ashwin/Desktop/LMS/render.yaml) at the repository root defining both services:
1. **Frontend**: Static Site, root `client`, build command `npm install && npm run build`, publish directory `dist`, with SPA rewrite rule `/* -> /index.html`.
2. **Backend**: Web Service, root `server`, build command `npm install && npx prisma generate`, start command `node src/server.js`, health check path `/api/v1/health`.

